# Pre-commit verification (always on)

Hosted GitHub Actions are parked to avoid runner charges. Local suites are the merge gate.

Before every `git commit`:

1. Run `pnpm hooks:install` so `scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit` is the repository hook path.
2. Run `pnpm precommit:verify`, or let the git hook run it.
3. Do not use `--no-verify`, `GIT_SKIP_HOOKS`, or any skip flag.
4. Do not treat skipped, filtered, or not-run suites as passed.
5. Do not re-enable `pull_request`, `push`, `schedule`, or other automatic triggers on `.github/workflows/*`.
6. Keep `OPENAI_API_KEY` empty. Do not make paid provider calls.

`pnpm precommit:verify` runs repository boundary, source integrity, format, lint, typecheck, Phase 1.3.5 parking/deployment contracts, and `verify:phase2.0` through `verify:phase3.4a`, then secret scan and inventory. Windows also runs the Phase 1.3.5 local-storage audit. Playwright, hosted PostgreSQL, Docker image builds, full Windows-owned owner-tool unit files, and history secret scan are not part of the commit hook.

If the hook is missing, install it and run the suite yourself before committing. A commit that bypasses the suite is incomplete.
